# KRAN skeleton & loading UI

## Canonical library

**Use:** `@/shared/components/skeleton` (also re-exported from `@/shared/components`).

**Do not** create duplicate skeleton components under domains or new `animate-pulse` layout blocks when a shared variant exists.

| Scenario | Component |
|----------|-----------|
| Single placeholder block | `SkeletonBlock` |
| Accessible wrapper | `SkeletonRegion` (`aria-busy`, one sr-only message) |
| Forms | `FormSkeleton` |
| Tables | `TableSkeleton`, `ProbityTablePageSkeleton`, `ProbityTableSkeletonBody` |
| Dashboard metrics | `DashboardMetricsSkeleton`, `MetricCardSkeleton` |
| Reports (generate flow) | `ReportResultsSkeleton` |
| Split filter + results | `SplitPanelSkeleton` |
| Full listing page | `PageCardSkeleton` (`variant`: `table` \| `form` \| `profile` only) |

Primitives: `SkeletonTextLines`, `SkeletonHeading`, `SkeletonCircle`, `SkeletonButton`, `SkeletonInput`, `SkeletonImage`, etc. — compose rather than one-off divs.

**Legacy:** `src/shared/components/skeletons/*` (login, home, seat selection) — page-specific; do not copy that pattern for module CRUD.

**Legacy shim:** `SkeletonBar` in `ui/Shimmer.jsx` delegates to `SkeletonBlock` — prefer `SkeletonBlock` in new code.

## Behavior

- Show skeletons **only while loading**; replace with content, empty state, or error when the request completes.
- Respect **`prefers-reduced-motion`** via `SKELETON_PULSE_CLASS` / `animate={false}` on `SkeletonBlock`.
- One **`SkeletonRegion`** per loading section — do not announce every line to screen readers.
- Match responsive layout of real content (same grid breakpoints as dashboards/tables).

## Workbench

Document and demo skeletons on **`/component-workbench/feedback/loading-states`** (`LoadingStatesFeedbackPage.jsx`). Update this page when adding public skeleton variants.

## When not to use skeletons

Short button actions → inline spinner on the control. Indeterminate long jobs → keep existing progress UX if already present. Failed requests → error UI, not endless skeleton.
